  "prefLabel": "Per-A 207.07 Sequestering of Witnesses",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Per-A 207.07 Sequestering of Witnesses. Either party may move to have the witnesses sequestered. However, the appointing authority, the appointing authority's designee, and the employee and director of personnel, if a party to the appeal, shall not be sequestered even if they are expected to testify.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Per-A 200) #7378, eff 10-23-00; ss by #9205, eff 10-23-08",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/per-a100-200.html"
